#### r5u-negated-jump — 2R.5 (gate): a modified jump is unmeasured — `JMP l S=` is the one stored, built and run
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  NOT JMP Done := c;
END_NETWORK
NETWORK LABEL: Done
  x := TRUE;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a modified jump or return

#### r5u-rising-jump — 2R.5 (gate): an edge on a jump is unmeasured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  R_EDGE JMP Done := c;
END_NETWORK
NETWORK LABEL: Done
  x := TRUE;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a modified jump or return

#### r5u-reset-jump — 2R.5 (gate): R= on a jump is unmeasured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  JMP Done R= c;
END_NETWORK
NETWORK LABEL: Done
  x := TRUE;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a modified jump or return

#### r5u-negated-return — 2R.5 (gate): a negated return is unmeasured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  NOT RETURN := c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a modified jump or return

#### r5u-falling-return-beside-a-coil — 2R.5 (gate): an edge on a return beside a coil is unmeasured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := F_EDGE RETURN := c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a modified jump or return

#### r5u-edge-set-coil — 2R.5 (gate): an edge on a set coil is unmeasured — `R_EDGE x :=` is the one measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  R_EDGE xe S= c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED an edge on a negated, set or reset coil

#### r5u-edge-negated-coil — 2R.5 (gate): an edge on a negated coil is unmeasured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  F_EDGE NOT xe := c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED an edge on a negated, set or reset coil

#### r5u-edge-en — 2R.5 (gate): an edge on the EN pin is unmeasured — `NOT EN c` is the one measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION FBD
NETWORK
  MOVE 5 => y R_EDGE EN c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED an edge on the EN pin

#### r5u-edge-negated-pin — 2R.5 (gate): an edge with a negation on one pin is unmeasured — each alone is measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION FBD
NETWORK
  x := AND(F_EDGE NOT IN1 := c, one);
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED an edge on a negated pin

#### r5u-negated-empty-branch — 2R.5 (gate): a negated empty slot is measured as a coil's value only
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := s BRANCH (NOT ,
                 b);
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a negated empty slot outside a lone plain coil's value

#### r5u-negated-empty-jump-value — 2R.5 (gate): a jump's negated empty value is unmeasured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  JMP Done := NOT ;
END_NETWORK
NETWORK LABEL: Done
  x := TRUE;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a negated empty slot outside a lone plain coil's value

#### r5u-split-reads-itself — 2R.5 (gate): a split read inside its own definition is unmeasured (#19 is a reference in another item)
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  split1 := split1 AND a;
  x := split1;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED read inside its own definition

#### r5u-split-defined-inside-itself — 2R.5 (gate): a split defined inside its own definition is defined twice
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  split1 := (split1 := a) AND b;
  x := split1;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_DUPLICATE_NAME defined twice

#### r5u-negated-coil-in-a-fan-out — 2R.5 (gate 2): a negated coil beside another coil is unmeasured — `NOT x :=` alone is measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  y := NOT xn := c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a negated or edge coil beside another coil

